<title>NETHERLANDS: TABLE - ASM LITHOGRAPHY H1 NET NLG 147 MLN.</title>
<headline>TABLE - ASM LITHOGRAPHY H1 NET NLG 147 MLN.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>First half of 1997</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>  Net per shr incl extraordinaries (guilders)   2.13 vs   1.49</p>
<p>  Net per shr excl extraordinaries (guilders)   1.68 vs   ----</p>
<p>  Net profit					    147.0  vs 100.7</p>
<p>  Extraordinary income				 31.1  vs  ----</p>
<p>  Turnover						766.5  vs 597.2</p>
<p>  Operating profit				    209.5  vs 155.1</p>
<p>  Tax							63.5  vs  55.2</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had expected ASM Lithography to report a net</p>
<p>profit from ordinary activities of 95-110 million guilders.</p>
<p>First-half profit figures for 1997 include extraordinary</p>
<p>income of 31.1 million guilders from the sale of a stake in one</p>
<p>of the company's suppliers.</p>
<p>ASM Lithography makes equipment for the production of</p>
<p>semiconductors and is 23.9 percent owned by Philips Electronics</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
